<!-- story: docs/stories/recipes-and-costing-redesign-prompt.story.md -->
<article class="recipes-costing">
	<section class="hero" aria-labelledby="recipes-costing-heading">
		<div class="container-page hero-grid">
			<div class="hero-copy anim-enter">
				<nav aria-label="Breadcrumb" class="feature-breadcrumb">
					<a href="/features">Every feature</a>
					<span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
					<span>Recipes and costing</span>
				</nav>
				<h1 id="recipes-costing-heading" class="feature-display">Cost a recipe before you quote.</h1>
				<p class="hero-lede">Ingredients, amounts, method and food cost live on one recipe. Start with one dish and what you pay for its ingredients today. Scale the portions and the original stays as you wrote it.</p>
				<div class="hero-actions">
					<a href={cta.href} target={cta.target} rel={cta.rel} aria-label={cta.ariaLabel} class="btn-primary">
						{cta.label}
					</a>
					<a
						href={demoCta.href}
						target={demoCta.target}
						rel={demoCta.rel}
						aria-label={demoCta.ariaLabel}
						class="btn-quiet"
					>
						{demoCta.label}
					</a>
				</div>
				<FeatureTrialTerms />
			</div>

			<figure class="record-flow anim-enter" style="--enter-delay: 120ms">
				<p class="figure-note">Illustrative recipe flow</p>
				<div class="record-pair">
					<div class="record recipe-record">
						<div class="record-head">
							<span>Working recipe</span>
							<span>24 portions</span>
						</div>
						<strong class="record-title">Herb roast chicken</strong>
						<dl class="record-facts">
							<div><dt>Yield</dt><dd>9 lb cooked</dd></div>
							<div><dt>Portion</dt><dd>6 oz</dd></div>
						</dl>
						<div class="record-rule"></div>
						<p class="record-label">Ingredients</p>
						<ul role="list" class="ingredient-lines">
							<!-- The product tour's recipe (src/lib/tour.ts), in US units and one
							     weight throughout (chef audit 2026-10-07: 7.8 kg here, 6.4 kg in
							     the builder below). -->
							<li><span>Chicken thigh, trimmed</span><strong>12 lb</strong></li>
							<li><span>Herb marinade</span><strong>2.4 lb</strong></li>
							<li><span>Lemon</span><strong>12 each</strong></li>
							<li><span>Pan jus</span><strong>1.5 qt</strong></li>
						</ul>
						<p class="method-line">Roast, rest, portion, and hold for service.</p>
					</div>

					<div class="flow-join" aria-hidden="true"><span></span></div>

					<div class="record costing-record">
						<div class="record-head">
							<span>Recipe costing</span>
							<span>Same recipe</span>
						</div>
						<strong class="record-title">Herb roast chicken</strong>
						<dl class="cost-facts">
							<div><dt>Recipe cost</dt><dd>$64.69</dd></div>
							<div><dt>Per portion</dt><dd>$2.70</dd></div>
							<div><dt>Food cost</dt><dd>30.0%</dd></div>
						</dl>
						<div class="record-rule"></div>
						<p class="record-label">The path stays visible</p>
						<ul role="list" class="cost-lines">
							<li><span>Purchased amount</span><strong>13.2 lb</strong></li>
							<li><span>Trim yield</span><strong>91%</strong></li>
							<li><span>Cost contribution</span><strong>$46.02</strong></li>
						</ul>
					</div>
				</div>
				<figcaption>Illustrative values: $64.69 ÷ 24 = $2.70 food per portion. At a $9.00 selling price, that is 30.0% food cost. Food cost excludes labor, rentals, tax and profit.</figcaption>
			</figure>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="split-problem" aria-labelledby="split-heading">
		<div class="container-page problem-grid">
			<div data-reveal>
				<h2 id="split-heading">Right now one dish lives in three places.</h2>
				<p>
					The method is in a binder. The current case price is in a purchase record. The quote is
					waiting in a spreadsheet. That works fine until the kitchen and the client both need
					an answer the same afternoon.
				</p>
			</div>
			<figure class="handoff" data-reveal>
				<div class="handoff-step">
					<span>Recipe</span>
					<strong>What to make</strong>
				</div>
				<div class="handoff-gap" aria-label="A manual handoff separates the recipe from its current price">
					<svg width="42" height="18" viewBox="0 0 42 18" aria-hidden="true">
						<path d="M1 9h33M28 2l7 7-7 7" />
					</svg>
					<small>rekey</small>
				</div>
				<div class="handoff-step">
					<span>Price</span>
					<strong>What it costs</strong>
				</div>
				<div class="handoff-gap" aria-label="A second manual handoff separates the cost from the quote">
					<svg width="42" height="18" viewBox="0 0 42 18" aria-hidden="true">
						<path d="M1 9h33M28 2l7 7-7 7" />
					</svg>
					<small>recheck</small>
				</div>
				<div class="handoff-step">
					<span>Quote</span>
					<strong>What you say</strong>
				</div>
				<figcaption>The method and the math belong on the same recipe.</figcaption>
			</figure>
		</div>
	</section>

	<nav class="product-nav container-page" aria-label="On this page">
		<a href="#recipe-management">
			<span>Recipe management</span>
			<small>Build it once. Find it, scale it, and hand it to the kitchen.</small>
			<svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 10h13M11 5l5 5-5 5" /></svg>
		</a>
		<a href="#recipe-lifecycle">
			<span>Publishing and recipe history</span>
			<small>From a private draft to what the crew reads, with old versions still there.</small>
			<svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 10h13M11 5l5 5-5 5" /></svg>
		</a>
		<a href="#recipe-costing">
			<span>Recipe costing</span>
			<small>Follow the price from the case to the plate and the quote.</small>
			<svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 10h13M11 5l5 5-5 5" /></svg>
		</a>
	</nav>

	<section id="recipe-management" class="product-section management" aria-labelledby="management-heading">
		<div class="container-page">
			<div class="section-intro" data-reveal>
				<h2 id="management-heading">
					One recipe, from first draft to prep sheet.
				</h2>
				<p>
					Write the dish down while it is still in your hands. Ingredients, prep, yield,
					sub-recipes and the version the kitchen should cook from all stay on one recipe.
				</p>
			</div>

			<figure class="management-workspace" data-reveal>
				<div class="builder-panel">
					<div class="panel-bar">
						<div><span class="status-dot"></span> Working recipe</div>
						<span>Private draft</span>
					</div>
					<div class="builder-title">
						<div>
							<small>Recipe name</small>
							<strong>Herb roast chicken</strong>
						</div>
						<div>
							<small>Batch yield</small>
							<strong>24 portions</strong>
						</div>
					</div>
					<div class="builder-table" role="table" aria-label="Illustrative recipe builder">
						<div class="builder-row builder-head" role="row">
							<span role="columnheader">Ingredient</span><span role="columnheader">Used</span><span role="columnheader">Prep</span>
						</div>
						<div class="builder-row" role="row"><span role="cell">Chicken thigh</span><strong role="cell">12 lb</strong><span role="cell">trimmed</span></div>
						<div class="builder-row active" role="row"><span role="cell">Herb marinade</span><strong role="cell">2.4 lb</strong><span role="cell">sub-recipe</span></div>
						<div class="builder-row" role="row"><span role="cell">Lemon</span><strong role="cell">12 each</strong><span role="cell">zested</span></div>
						<div class="builder-row add-row" role="row"><span role="cell">Add an ingredient</span><span role="cell"></span><span role="cell">Type, pick, next line</span></div>
					</div>
				</div>

				<div class="management-side">
					<div class="scale-preview">
						<div class="panel-bar"><div>Scaling preview</div><span>Saved recipe unchanged</span></div>
						<div class="scale-change">
							<div><small>Original</small><strong>24</strong><span>portions</span></div>
							<svg width="34" height="18" viewBox="0 0 34 18" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M1 9h26M22 3l6 6-6 6" /></svg>
							<div><small>Target</small><strong>80</strong><span>portions</span></div>
						</div>
						<p>Chicken thigh <strong>40 lb</strong></p>
						<p>Herb marinade <strong>8 lb</strong></p>
					</div>
					<div class="print-preview">
						<div class="print-stamp">Printed 8:42 AM</div>
						<strong>Herb roast chicken</strong>
						<p>Roast until browned. Rest before portioning.</p>
						<div class="print-rule"></div>
						<small>24 portions · 6 oz each</small>
					</div>
				</div>
				<figcaption>Illustrative walkthrough of shipped recipe-builder, scaling-preview, and print-sheet behavior.</figcaption>
			</figure>

			<div class="feature-scenes">
				<article>
					<h3>Build without leaving the recipe.</h3>
					<p>Type, pick, next line. Missing an ingredient? Add it right there without losing what you have built.</p>
				</article>
				<article>
					<h3>Scale it and leave the original alone.</h3>
					<p>Preview a bigger or smaller batch, or work from what you have on hand. The saved recipe stays exactly as you left it.</p>
				</article>
				<article>
					<h3>Print the version the kitchen cooks from.</h3>
					<p>The kitchen sheet prints with the time on it, so the paper on the prep table tells you how old it is.</p>
				</article>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section id="recipe-lifecycle" class="product-section lifecycle" aria-labelledby="lifecycle-heading">
		<div class="container-page">
			<div class="section-intro" data-reveal>
				<h2 id="lifecycle-heading">You pick the version the kitchen cooks from.</h2>
				<p>Build it in private. Once it passes the ready check, you publish it, and the crew gets a kitchen view they can read but not edit. Earlier published versions stay there when you need to see what changed.</p>
			</div>
			<figure class="lifecycle-path" data-reveal>
				<ol role="list">
					{recipeLifecycle.map((step, index) => (
						<li><span>{String(index + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span><strong>{step.name}</strong><p>{step.detail}</p></li>
					))}
				</ol>
				<figcaption>Owners can also archive and restore. Neither one erases the published history.</figcaption>
			</figure>
			<div class="filing-strip" data-reveal>
				<div><h3>File it the way the kitchen looks for it.</h3><p>Collections, tags, stations and shelves. When the book gets big, there is more than one way back to a recipe.</p></div>
				<ul role="list"><li>Collections</li><li>Tags</li><li>Stations</li><li>Shelves</li></ul>
				<div><h3>Keep the method in steps.</h3><p>Structured method steps move up and down, so the method never turns into one long paragraph.</p></div>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section id="recipe-costing" class="product-section costing" aria-labelledby="costing-heading">
		<div class="container-page">
			<div class="section-intro costing-intro" data-reveal>
				<h2 id="costing-heading">
					Catch a cost change before it reaches the quote.
				</h2>
				<p>
					A case price tells you little until the pack size, the usable yield, the sub-recipe,
					the portion and the head count have had their say. Every step stays open so you can check it.
				</p>
			</div>

			<figure class="cost-path" data-reveal>
				<ol role="list">
					{costPath.map((step, index) => (
						<li>
							<div class="cost-index">{index + 1}</div>
							<strong>{step.name}</strong>
							<p>{step.note}</p>
						</li>
					))}
				</ol>
				<figcaption>Case price to event cost. When a number looks off, every step is there to check.</figcaption>
			</figure>

			<div class="costing-evidence">
				<div class="evidence-copy" data-reveal>
					<h3>Show the math.</h3>
					<p>
						What you bought, the yield, how much to buy, the prep state and what the line adds to
						the cost all sit together. Open any of it and trace the number back.
					</p>
					<ul role="list">
						<li>Missing prices are named instead of reading as zero.</li>
						<li>Every line adds up to the recipe total.</li>
						<li>Trim and cooking loss remain separate facts.</li>
					</ul>
				</div>
				<figure class="screenshot-frame" data-reveal>
					<picture>
						<source media="(max-width: 63.99rem)" srcset="/proof/yield-lines-mobile.png" width="748" height="1102" />
						<img
							src="/proof/yield-lines.png"
							width="1490"
							height="1042"
							loading="lazy"
							decoding="async"
							alt="A CostCook recipe line, Roma tomato: 2.1 oz at 91% yield, 2.3 oz to buy, 12% of cost, $0.17. Opened, it shows its working: 2.1 oz usable quantity, trim yield 91%, required as purchased 2.1 oz ÷ 0.91 = 2.3 oz, a 25 lb case at $29.14, line cost $0.17, and the recorded purchase it came from."
						/>
					</picture>
					<figcaption>Each ingredient carries its own working, not just a share of the final total.</figcaption>
				</figure>
			</div>

			<div class="quote-evidence" data-reveal>
				<figure>
					<picture>
						<source media="(max-width: 63.99rem)" srcset="/proof/order-price-today-mobile.png" width="780" height="1358" />
						<img
							src="/proof/order-price-today.png"
							width="1888"
							height="722"
							loading="lazy"
							decoding="async"
							alt="A confirmed wedding order for 150 guests, prices locked: $95.00 a guest, locked when confirmed; food cost 27.6% against a 30% target, food $26.18 a guest; and today's ingredient prices, unchanged since it was quoted."
						/>
					</picture>
				</figure>
				<div>
					<h3>Price the menu before you commit.</h3>
					<p>
						See cost per guest next to what you plan to charge. Once the order is confirmed, hold
						the frozen quote up against today's prices.
					</p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="connected-proof" aria-labelledby="connected-heading">
		<div class="container-page proof-grid">
			<div data-reveal>
				<h2 id="connected-heading">A sauce is one recipe, even in five dishes.</h2>
				<p>
					Cost the batch once and use it wherever it goes. When something in it changes, you see
					which recipes and menus it touches before you decide what to do.
				</p>
			</div>
			<figure class="subrecipe-map" data-reveal>
				<div class="source-recipe">
					<span>Sub-recipe</span>
					<strong>Herb marinade</strong>
					<small>One batch · one cost</small>
				</div>
				<div class="map-rule" aria-hidden="true"></div>
				<ul role="list">
					{dishes.map((dish) => <li>{dish}</li>)}
				</ul>
				<figcaption>One sauce in five dishes, costed in one place.</figcaption>
			</figure>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="capabilities" aria-labelledby="capabilities-heading">
		<div class="container-page">
			<div class="capability-heading" data-reveal>
				<div>
					<h2 id="capabilities-heading">What is in Recipes & Costing.</h2>
					<p>Open the details to check what is available today.</p>
				</div>
				<p class="count"><strong>{capabilityCount}</strong><span>shipped capabilities</span></p>
			</div>

			<div class="disclosures">
				{capabilities.map((group) => (
					<details id={`features-${group.id}`} data-reveal>
						<summary>
							<span><strong>{group.kicker}</strong><small>{group.title}</small></span>
							<span class="summary-count">{group.items.length}</span>
							<svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 7l6 6 6-6" /></svg>
						</summary>
						<ul role="list">
							{group.items.map((item) => (
								<li><strong>{item.lead}</strong> <span>{item.detail}</span></li>
							))}
						</ul>
					</details>
				))}
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="faq" aria-labelledby="faq-heading">
		<div class="container-page faq-grid">
			<div class="faq-intro" data-reveal>
				<h2 id="faq-heading">Frequently asked questions</h2>
				<p>What people ask before they bring a real recipe in.</p>
			</div>

			<div class="faq-list">
				{faqItems.map((item) => (
					<details data-reveal>
						<summary>
							<span>{item.question}</span>
							<svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" aria-hidden="true">
								<path d="M4 7l6 6 6-6" />
							</svg>
						</summary>
						<p>{item.answer}</p>
					</details>
				))}
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="closing" aria-labelledby="closing-heading">
		<div class="container-page closing-grid" data-reveal>
			<div>
				<h2 id="closing-heading">Start with the dish you sell most.</h2>
				<p>Bring one real menu and follow it from recipe to quote, with the math showing.</p>
			</div>
			<div class="closing-actions">
				<a href={cta.href} target={cta.target} rel={cta.rel} aria-label={cta.ariaLabel} class="btn-primary">
					{cta.label}
				</a>
				<a
					href={demoCta.href}
					target={demoCta.target}
					rel={demoCta.rel}
					aria-label={demoCta.ariaLabel}
					class="btn-quiet"
				>
					{demoCta.label}
				</a>
			</div>
		</div>
		<nav class="container-page onward feature-onward" aria-label="Related feature guides">
			<a href="/features/menus-and-quotes">Menus &amp; quotes</a>
			<a href="/features">See every CostCook feature</a>
		</nav>
	</section>
</article>

<style>
	.recipes-costing {
		--record-rule: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-ink) 18%, transparent);
		overflow: clip;
	}

	.hero {
		border-block: 1px solid var(--color-hairline);
		background: var(--color-cream);
	}

	.hero-grid {
		display: grid;
		gap: clamp(3rem, 6vw, 6.5rem);
		align-items: center;
		padding-block: clamp(4rem, 7vw, 7.5rem);
	}

	.hero h1 {
		max-width: 11.5ch;
		margin-top: 1.5rem;
	}

	.hero-lede {
		max-width: 55ch;
		margin-top: 1.75rem;
		font-size: var(--text-lede);
		line-height: 1.55;
		color: var(--color-ink-soft);
	}

	.hero-actions,
	.closing-actions {
		display: flex;
		flex-wrap: wrap;
		gap: 0.85rem;
		margin-top: 2rem;
	}

	.record-flow {
		position: relative;
		min-width: 0;
	}

	.figure-note {
		margin-bottom: 0.7rem;
		font-size: var(--text-label-sm);
		font-weight: 600;
		letter-spacing: 0.08em;
		text-transform: uppercase;
		color: var(--color-amber-deep);
	}

	.record-pair {
		display: grid;
		gap: 1.25rem;
	}

	.record {
		position: relative;
		min-width: 0;
		padding: clamp(1.2rem, 3vw, 1.8rem);
		background: var(--color-paper);
		box-shadow: var(--shadow-ticket);
	}

	.recipe-record {
		border-top: 3px solid var(--color-green);
	}

	.costing-record {
		border-top: 3px solid var(--color-amber-deep);
	}

	.record-head {
		display: flex;
		justify-content: space-between;
		gap: 1rem;
		font-size: var(--text-micro);
		font-weight: 700;
		letter-spacing: 0.08em;
		text-transform: uppercase;
		color: var(--color-ink-soft);
	}

	.record .record-title {
		display: block;
		margin-top: 0.85rem;
		font-family: var(--font-display);
		font-size: var(--text-record);
		font-weight: 600;
	}

	.record-facts,
	.cost-facts {
		display: grid;
		gap: 0.75rem;
		margin-top: 1rem;
	}

	.record-facts {
		grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
	}

	.cost-facts {
		/* Two columns keep adjacent currency amounts distinct in the narrow record. */
		grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
	}

	.record-facts div,
	.cost-facts div {
		min-width: 0;
	}

	.record dt,
	.record-label {
		font-size: var(--text-micro);
		font-weight: 700;
		letter-spacing: 0.08em;
		text-transform: uppercase;
		color: var(--color-ink-soft);
	}

	.record dd {
		margin-top: 0.2rem;
		font-weight: 700;
		font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
	}

	.record-rule {
		height: 1px;
		margin-block: 1rem;
		background: var(--record-rule);
	}

	.ingredient-lines,
	.cost-lines {
		margin-top: 0.5rem;
	}

	.ingredient-lines li,
	.cost-lines li {
		display: flex;
		flex-wrap: wrap;
		justify-content: space-between;
		gap: 1rem;
		padding-block: 0.28rem;
		border-bottom: 1px solid var(--record-rule);
		font-size: var(--text-caption);
	}

	.ingredient-lines strong,
	.cost-lines strong {
		font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
		white-space: nowrap;
	}

	.method-line {
		margin-top: 0.9rem;
		font-size: var(--text-label-sm);
		line-height: 1.45;
		color: var(--color-ink-soft);
	}

	.flow-join {
		display: none;
	}

	.record-flow figcaption,
	.management-workspace > figcaption,
	.screenshot-frame figcaption,
	.subrecipe-map figcaption {
		margin-top: 0.85rem;
		font-size: var(--text-label-sm);
		line-height: 1.5;
		color: var(--color-ink-soft);
	}

	.split-problem {
		background: var(--color-ink);
		color: var(--color-offwhite);
	}

	.problem-grid {
		display: grid;
		gap: 3rem;
		align-items: center;
		padding-block: var(--spacing-section-tight);
	}

	.problem-grid h2,
	.section-intro h2,
	.connected-proof h2,
	.capability-heading h2,
	.closing h2 {
		font-size: var(--text-h2);
		font-weight: 600;
	}

	.problem-grid p {
		max-width: 58ch;
		margin-top: 1.25rem;
		line-height: 1.65;
		color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-offwhite) 75%, transparent);
	}

	.handoff {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: 1fr auto 1fr auto 1fr;
		align-items: center;
		gap: 0.75rem;
	}

	.handoff-step {
		min-width: 0;
		padding-block: 1rem;
		border-block: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-offwhite) 30%, transparent);
	}

	.handoff-step span {
		display: block;
		font-size: var(--text-label-sm);
		letter-spacing: 0.1em;
		text-transform: uppercase;
		color: var(--color-amber-light);
	}

	.handoff-step strong {
		display: block;
		margin-top: 0.35rem;
		font-family: var(--font-display);
		font-size: var(--text-body-lg);
	}

	.handoff-gap {
		text-align: center;
		color: var(--color-amber-light);
	}

	.handoff-gap svg,
	.product-nav svg,
	.scale-change svg,
	.disclosures svg {
		fill: none;
		stroke: currentColor;
		stroke-width: 1.5;
		stroke-linecap: round;
		stroke-linejoin: round;
	}

	.handoff-gap small {
		display: block;
		font-size: var(--text-micro);
		letter-spacing: 0.05em;
	}

	.handoff figcaption {
		grid-column: 1 / -1;
		margin-top: 1rem;
		font-family: var(--font-display);
		font-size: var(--text-record-sm);
		color: var(--color-offwhite);
	}

	.product-nav {
		display: grid;
		padding-block: 0;
		background: var(--color-offwhite);
	}

	.product-nav a {
		position: relative;
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: 1fr auto;
		gap: 0.35rem 1rem;
		min-height: 112px;
		align-content: center;
		padding: 1.5rem clamp(1rem, 3vw, 2rem);
		border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-ticket-rule);
		color: var(--color-ink);
		transition: background-color 150ms ease-out;
	}

	@media (hover: hover) {
		.product-nav a:hover {
			background: var(--color-softgreen);
		}
	}

	.product-nav span {
		font-family: var(--font-display);
		font-size: var(--text-record-sm);
		font-weight: 600;
	}

	.product-nav small {
		grid-column: 1;
		max-width: 44ch;
		font-size: var(--text-caption);
		line-height: 1.45;
		color: var(--color-ink-soft);
	}

	.product-nav svg {
		grid-row: 1 / span 2;
		grid-column: 2;
		align-self: center;
		color: var(--color-green-deep);
	}

	.product-section {
		scroll-margin-top: 1rem;
		padding-block: var(--spacing-section);
	}

	.management {
		border-top: 1px solid var(--color-hairline);
		background: var(--color-softgreen);
	}

	.lifecycle { background: var(--color-paper); }

	.costing {
		background: var(--color-cream);
	}

	.section-intro {
		display: grid;
		gap: 1.25rem;
		align-items: end;
	}

	.section-intro h2 {
		max-width: 19ch;
	}

	.section-intro > p {
		max-width: 57ch;
		font-size: var(--text-lede);
		line-height: 1.55;
		color: var(--color-ink-soft);
	}

	.management-workspace {
		display: grid;
		gap: 1.25rem;
		margin-top: clamp(3rem, 6vw, 5rem);
	}

	.builder-panel,
	.scale-preview,
	.print-preview {
		background: var(--color-paper);
		box-shadow: var(--shadow-ticket);
	}

	.builder-panel {
		min-width: 0;
		padding: clamp(1rem, 3vw, 1.75rem);
	}

	.panel-bar {
		display: flex;
		justify-content: space-between;
		gap: 1rem;
		padding-bottom: 0.85rem;
		border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-hairline);
		font-size: var(--text-label-sm);
		font-weight: 700;
		letter-spacing: 0.06em;
		text-transform: uppercase;
		color: var(--color-ink-soft);
	}

	.status-dot {
		display: inline-block;
		width: 0.55rem;
		height: 0.55rem;
		margin-right: 0.4rem;
		border-radius: 50%;
		background: var(--color-green);
	}

	.builder-title {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) auto;
		gap: 2rem;
		padding-block: 1.5rem;
	}

	.builder-title small,
	.scale-change small {
		display: block;
		font-size: var(--text-micro);
		font-weight: 700;
		letter-spacing: 0.06em;
		text-transform: uppercase;
		color: var(--color-ink-soft);
	}

	.builder-title strong {
		display: block;
		margin-top: 0.25rem;
		font-family: var(--font-display);
		font-size: var(--text-record-sm);
	}

	.builder-row {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 0.35fr) minmax(0, 0.6fr);
		gap: 1rem;
		align-items: center;
		padding: 0.85rem;
		border-top: 1px solid var(--color-hairline);
		font-size: var(--text-caption);
	}

	.builder-head {
		padding-block: 0.55rem;
		border-top: 0;
		background: var(--color-offwhite);
		font-size: var(--text-micro);
		font-weight: 700;
		letter-spacing: 0.06em;
		text-transform: uppercase;
		color: var(--color-ink-soft);
	}

	.builder-row.active {
		background: var(--color-softgreen);
	}

	.builder-row strong {
		font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
	}

	.add-row {
		color: var(--color-green-deep);
		font-weight: 600;
	}

	.management-side {
		display: grid;
		gap: 1.25rem;
	}

	.scale-preview,
	.print-preview {
		padding: 1.35rem;
	}

	.scale-change {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) auto minmax(0, 1fr);
		gap: 0.75rem;
		align-items: center;
		margin-block: 1.4rem;
	}

	.scale-change strong {
		display: block;
		font-family: var(--font-display);
		font-size: var(--text-h2);
		font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
	}

	.scale-change span,
	.scale-preview p {
		font-size: var(--text-label-sm);
		color: var(--color-ink-soft);
	}

	.scale-preview p {
		display: flex;
		justify-content: space-between;
		gap: 1rem;
		padding-block: 0.35rem;
		border-top: 1px solid var(--color-hairline);
	}

	.print-preview {
		position: relative;
		border-top: 3px solid var(--color-amber-deep);
	}

	.print-stamp {
		font-size: var(--text-micro);
		font-weight: 700;
		letter-spacing: 0.05em;
		text-transform: uppercase;
		color: var(--color-amber-deep);
	}

	.print-preview > strong {
		display: block;
		margin-top: 1rem;
		font-family: var(--font-display);
		font-size: var(--text-record);
	}

	.print-preview p,
	.print-preview small {
		margin-top: 0.75rem;
		font-size: var(--text-caption);
		line-height: 1.5;
		color: var(--color-ink-soft);
	}

	.print-rule {
		height: 1px;
		margin-top: 1rem;
		background: var(--color-ticket-rule);
	}

	.feature-scenes {
		display: grid;
		gap: 2rem;
		margin-top: 3rem;
	}

	.feature-scenes article {
		padding-top: 1.2rem;
		border-top: 1px solid var(--color-hairline-strong);
	}

	.feature-scenes h3,
	.costing-evidence h3,
	.quote-evidence h3 {
		font-size: var(--text-h3);
		font-weight: 600;
	}

	.feature-scenes p,
	.filing-strip p,
	.costing-evidence p,
	.quote-evidence p {
		margin-top: 0.75rem;
		line-height: 1.65;
		color: var(--color-ink-soft);
	}

	.lifecycle-path { margin-top: clamp(3rem, 6vw, 5rem); padding: clamp(1.25rem, 3vw, 2rem); border-block: 1px solid var(--color-ticket-rule); background: var(--color-cream); }
	.lifecycle-path ol { display: grid; gap: 1rem; }
	.lifecycle-path li { padding-top: 1rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--record-rule); }
	.lifecycle-path li > span { color: var(--color-amber-deep); font-size: var(--text-micro); font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
	.lifecycle-path strong { display: block; margin-top: .4rem; font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 1.35rem; }
	.lifecycle-path li p { margin-top: .45rem; color: var(--color-ink-soft); font-size: .84rem; line-height: 1.5; }
	.lifecycle-path figcaption { margin-top: 1.5rem; padding-top: 1rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--record-rule); color: var(--color-ink-soft); font-size: .82rem; }
	.filing-strip { display: grid; gap: 2rem; margin-top: clamp(3rem, 6vw, 5rem); }
	.filing-strip > div { padding-top: 1.2rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--color-hairline-strong); }
	.filing-strip h3 { font-size: var(--text-h3); font-weight: 600; }
	.filing-strip ul { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr)); border-top: 1px solid var(--color-ticket-rule); }
	.filing-strip li { padding: .9rem .75rem .9rem 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-ticket-rule); color: var(--color-green-deep); font-weight: 700; }

	.cost-path {
		margin-top: clamp(3rem, 6vw, 5rem);
		padding: clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 2.75rem);
		background: var(--color-ink);
		color: var(--color-offwhite);
	}

	.cost-path ol {
		display: grid;
		gap: 1.5rem;
	}

	.cost-path li {
		position: relative;
		padding-top: 1rem;
		border-top: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-offwhite) 30%, transparent);
	}

	.cost-index {
		font-size: var(--text-label-sm);
		font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
		color: var(--color-amber-light);
	}

	.cost-path strong {
		display: block;
		margin-top: 0.45rem;
		font-family: var(--font-display);
		font-size: var(--text-record-sm);
	}

	.cost-path p {
		margin-top: 0.55rem;
		font-size: var(--text-caption);
		line-height: 1.5;
		color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-offwhite) 72%, transparent);
	}

	.cost-path figcaption {
		margin-top: 1.5rem;
		padding-top: 1rem;
		border-top: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-offwhite) 30%, transparent);
		font-size: var(--text-caption);
		color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-offwhite) 78%, transparent);
	}

	.costing-evidence,
	.quote-evidence {
		display: grid;
		gap: 2rem;
		align-items: center;
		margin-top: clamp(3.5rem, 8vw, 7rem);
	}

	.evidence-copy ul {
		margin-top: 1.5rem;
	}

	.evidence-copy li {
		padding-block: 0.65rem;
		border-top: 1px solid var(--color-ticket-rule);
		font-size: var(--text-body-sm);
	}

	.screenshot-frame {
		min-width: 0;
	}

	.screenshot-frame picture {
		display: block;
		padding: clamp(0.5rem, 1.3vw, 0.85rem);
		background: var(--color-paper);
		box-shadow: var(--shadow-ticket);
	}

	.screenshot-frame img,
	.quote-evidence img {
		display: block;
		width: 100%;
		height: auto;
	}

	.quote-evidence {
		padding-top: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3.5rem);
		border-top: 1px solid var(--color-ticket-rule);
	}

	.quote-evidence figure {
		overflow: hidden;
		background: var(--color-ink);
		box-shadow: var(--shadow-ticket);
	}

	.connected-proof {
		padding-block: var(--spacing-section);
		background: var(--color-paper);
	}

	.proof-grid {
		display: grid;
		gap: clamp(3rem, 7vw, 6rem);
		align-items: center;
	}

	.connected-proof h2 {
		max-width: 13ch;
	}

	.connected-proof p {
		max-width: 52ch;
		margin-top: 1.25rem;
		line-height: 1.65;
		color: var(--color-ink-soft);
	}

	.subrecipe-map {
		position: relative;
		min-width: 0;
	}

	.source-recipe {
		position: relative;
		z-index: 1;
		width: min(100%, 18rem);
		margin-inline: auto;
		padding: 1.35rem;
		border-top: 3px solid var(--color-green);
		background: var(--color-softgreen);
		box-shadow: var(--shadow-ticket);
		text-align: center;
	}

	.source-recipe span,
	.source-recipe small {
		display: block;
		font-size: var(--text-label-sm);
		color: var(--color-ink-soft);
	}

	.source-recipe strong {
		display: block;
		margin-block: 0.35rem;
		font-family: var(--font-display);
		font-size: var(--text-record-sm);
	}

	.map-rule {
		width: 1px;
		height: 2rem;
		margin-inline: auto;
		background: var(--color-amber-deep);
	}

	.subrecipe-map ul {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
		gap: 1px;
		background: var(--color-ticket-rule);
		border: 1px solid var(--color-ticket-rule);
	}

	.subrecipe-map li {
		padding: 1rem;
		background: var(--color-cream);
		font-size: var(--text-caption);
		font-weight: 600;
		text-align: center;
	}

	.capabilities {
		padding-block: var(--spacing-section);
		border-top: 1px solid var(--color-hairline);
		background: var(--color-offwhite);
	}

	.capability-heading {
		display: flex;
		flex-wrap: wrap;
		justify-content: space-between;
		gap: 2rem;
		align-items: end;
	}

	.capability-heading > div > p {
		margin-top: 0.8rem;
		color: var(--color-ink-soft);
	}

	.count {
		display: flex;
		align-items: baseline;
		gap: 0.65rem;
		color: var(--color-ink-soft);
	}

	.count strong {
		font-family: var(--font-display);
		font-size: var(--text-h2);
		font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
		color: var(--color-amber-deep);
	}

	.count span {
		font-size: var(--text-label-sm);
	}

	.disclosures {
		margin-top: 3rem;
		border-top: 1px solid var(--color-ticket-rule);
	}

	.disclosures details {
		border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-ticket-rule);
	}

	.disclosures summary {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: 1fr auto auto;
		gap: 1rem;
		align-items: center;
		min-height: 76px;
		padding-block: 1rem;
		cursor: pointer;
		list-style: none;
	}

	.disclosures summary::-webkit-details-marker {
		display: none;
	}

	.disclosures summary > span:first-child {
		display: grid;
		gap: 0.2rem;
	}

	.disclosures summary strong {
		font-size: var(--text-body-lg);
	}

	.disclosures summary small {
		font-size: var(--text-label-sm);
		line-height: 1.4;
		color: var(--color-ink-soft);
	}

	.summary-count {
		font-size: var(--text-label-sm);
		font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
		color: var(--color-amber-deep);
	}

	.disclosures svg {
		transition: transform 180ms ease-out;
	}

	.disclosures details[open] svg {
		transform: rotate(180deg);
	}

	.disclosures ul {
		padding-bottom: 1.5rem;
		columns: 1;
	}

	.disclosures li {
		break-inside: avoid;
		padding-block: 0.65rem;
		border-top: 1px solid var(--color-hairline);
		font-size: var(--text-caption);
		line-height: 1.55;
	}

	.disclosures li span {
		color: var(--color-ink-soft);
	}

	.faq {
		padding-block: var(--spacing-section-tight);
		border-top: 1px solid var(--color-hairline);
		background: var(--color-paper);
	}

	.faq-grid {
		display: grid;
		gap: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 6rem);
	}

	.faq-intro p {
		max-width: 42ch;
		margin-top: 1rem;
		color: var(--color-ink-soft);
	}

	.faq-list {
		border-top: 1px solid var(--color-ticket-rule);
	}

	.faq-list details {
		border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-ticket-rule);
	}

	.faq-list summary {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) auto;
		gap: 1.5rem;
		align-items: center;
		min-height: 72px;
		padding-block: 1rem;
		cursor: pointer;
		list-style: none;
		font-weight: 650;
	}

	.faq-list summary::-webkit-details-marker {
		display: none;
	}

	.faq-list summary svg {
		color: var(--color-green-deep);
		transition: transform 180ms ease-out;
	}

	.faq-list summary path {
		fill: none;
		stroke: currentColor;
		stroke-width: 1.5;
	}

	.faq-list details[open] summary svg {
		transform: rotate(180deg);
	}

	.faq-list details > p {
		max-width: 66ch;
		padding: 0 3.25rem 1.5rem 0;
		line-height: 1.65;
		color: var(--color-ink-soft);
	}

	.closing {
		border-top: 1px solid var(--color-hairline-strong);
		background: var(--color-softgreen);
	}

	.closing-grid {
		display: grid;
		gap: 2rem;
		align-items: center;
		padding-block: var(--spacing-section-tight);
	}

	.closing p {
		max-width: 52ch;
		margin-top: 1rem;
		color: var(--color-ink-soft);
	}

	.closing-actions {
		margin-top: 0;
	}

	.onward {
		display: flex;
		flex-wrap: wrap;
		gap: 1rem 2rem;
		padding-block: 1.5rem;
		border-top: 1px solid var(--color-hairline-strong);
	}

	.onward a {
		display: inline-flex;
		min-height: 44px;
		align-items: center;
		color: var(--color-green-deep);
		font-weight: 600;
		text-decoration: underline;
		text-decoration-color: var(--color-hairline-strong);
		text-underline-offset: 4px;
	}

	/* REFLOW AT 200% TEXT (issue #79). A grid with no column template sizes
	   its one implicit track to its content's min-content width, so at 200%
	   text on a phone the hero and the product panels grew past the screen
	   and the article's overflow-x: clip cut their right edge off. One
	   shrinkable track below the breakpoints; the media rules below set the
	   wide layouts. Rows that pair a label and a value wrap instead of
